DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggggaatteecc utility is a network client for the GEOM Gate class.  It is
     responsible for the creation of ggggaattee devices and forwarding I/O requests
     between the GGEEOOMM GGaattee kernel subsystem and the ggated(8) network daemon.
     Available commands:

     ccrreeaattee   Connect to a ggated(8) daemon on the specified host and create a
              ggggaattee provider for the specified remote file or device.

     rreessccuuee   Create a new connection after the ggggaatteecc process has died or
              been killed.  The new connection to the ggated(8) daemon handles
              pending and future requests.

     ddeessttrrooyy  Destroy the given ggggaattee provider.

     lliisstt     List ggggaattee providers.

     Available options:

     --ff               Forcibly destroy ggggaattee provider (cancels all pending re‐
                      quests).

     --nn               Do not use TCP_NODELAY option on TCP sockets.

     --oo rroo | wwoo | rrww  Specify permissions to use when opening the file or de‐
                      vice: read-only (rroo), write-only (wwoo), or read-write
                      (rrww).  Default is rrww.

     --pp _p_o_r_t          Port to connect to on the remote host.  Default is 3080.

     --qq _q_u_e_u_e___s_i_z_e    Number of pending I/O requests that can be queued before
                      they will start to be canceled.  Default is 1024.

     --RR _r_c_v_b_u_f        Size of receive buffer to use.  Default is 131072
                      (128kB).

     --SS _s_n_d_b_u_f        Size of send buffer to use.  Default is 131072 (128kB).

     --ss _s_e_c_t_o_r_s_i_z_e    Sector size for ggggaattee provider.  If not specified, it is
                      taken from the device, or set to 512 bytes for files.

     --tt _t_i_m_e_o_u_t       Number of seconds to wait before an I/O request will be
                      canceled.  Default is 0, which means no timeout.

     --uu _u_n_i_t          Unit number to use.

     --vv               Do not fork, run in foreground and print debug informa‐
                      tion on standard output.

     _h_o_s_t             Remote host to connect to.

     _p_a_t_h             Path to a regular file or device.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     Exit status is 0 on success, or 1 if the command fails.  To get details
     about the failure, ggggaatteecc should be called with the --vv option.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Use a CD-ROM device on a remote host.

           server# cat /etc/gg.exports
           client RO /dev/cd0
           server# ggated

           client# ggatec create -o ro server /dev/cd0
           ggate0
           client# mount_cd9660 /dev/ggate0 /cdrom

